%N A393267 Array read by descending antidiagonals T(n,k) is the minimum total surface area of k-element sets of distinct integer-sided cuboids that fill an n X n X n cube.
%C A393267 The total surface area of k-element sets of cuboids is the sum of surface area of 2*(x*y+y*z+z*x) of each cuboid x X y X z in a set of distinct k cuboids.
%H A393267 Diego Lago Gómez, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.15894">The minimum surface area of k unequal boxes tiling a cube: sharp thresholds, a fault-free law, and a reduction to two dimensions</a>, arXiv:2607.15894 [math.CO], 2026. See pp. 2, 11 (Remark 22).
%F A393267 T(n,1) = 6*n^2.
%F A393267 T(n,2) = 8*n^2 for n > 2.
%F A393267 T(n,3) = 2*n*(4*n+1) for n > 2.
%F A393267 T(n,k) = 8*n^2 + 2*n + 2*(k-3) for k >= 4 and n >= (k-2)*(k-1)/2. - _Diego Lago Gómez_, Jul 12 2026
